# Messaging: Missed Incoming Calls, "Awaiting Prekey Material", Slow History (2026-07-03)

Cross-machine test (host + TestVM with the packaged installer) surfaced three
defects. All were root-caused with live DB evidence (service-role REST reads of
messaging_devices / messaging_signed_prekeys / messaging_call_signals).

## 1. Incoming video calls never rang on the callee
**Evidence:** ring/offer/ice rows from the VM (teslagreat101, device 5506f752)
sat in `messaging_call_signals` correctly targeted at threathunter369's device
c7a12249 — transport and device-targeting were fine; the callee just wasn't
listening. The signal subscription lived inside `useSecureCall`, which only
mounted with SecureChatPage (chat open AND workspace-unlocked).

**Fix:** app-level `CallProvider` (src/components/call/CallProvider.tsx),
mounted in App.tsx ABOVE the router and the workspace lock:
- owns the refactored `useSecureCall({ userId, deviceId })` engine; resolves
  the local device id itself (retried `keys_upload_identity_bundle`);
- `use-secure-call.ts` now derives all signal addressing from a `CallRoute` —
  outgoing: `startCall(peer, conversationId)`; incoming: conversation + caller
  ids + hybrid KEM ciphertext all come from the offer row, so answering works
  from ANY page (answering never unlocks chat history — Rust callee setup only
  needs auth + identity);
- renders IncomingCallModal + InCallOverlay globally; resolves caller display
  name from profiles; WebAudio two-tone ringtone (no asset; autoplay already
  allowed via WebView2 flag); `requestUserAttention` taskbar flash (new
  capability `core:window:allow-request-user-attention`);
- SecureChatPage consumes `useCall()` and only supplies the outgoing target.

## 2. "Awaiting prekey material" (device stranded with no active signed prekey)
**Evidence:** TG's older device c045b6c5 had its only signed-prekey row
`is_active=false` with no replacement — the rotation/publish flows ran
"deactivate old" BEFORE "publish new", so a failure between the two writes
left the device keyless → unsendable → unreachable for messages AND calls.

**Fix:** publish-first-then-deactivate in BOTH
`messaging-bootstrap.ts::ensureSignedPrekey` and
`KeyManagementPage::rotateAndPublishPrekey`. A transient two-active overlap is
harmless — the device join in use-dashboard-data already picks the newest by
created_at. Stranded devices self-heal on next launch/chat-open (bootstrap
re-upserts the local prekey active).

## 3. Slow "Loading encrypted history..." + composer stuck on "Sending"
Root causes: (a) `messaging_receive_encrypted_message` and
`messaging_send_encrypted_message` were SYNC Tauri commands → every decrypt ran
on the MAIN Rust thread (same class as the vault freeze); (b) hydration
decrypted every group sequentially, one awaited IPC at a time; (c) the
envelope query fetched the OLDEST 250 (`ascending+limit`) so long chats never
even showed recent messages; (d) plaintext caches were per-mount refs — every
page visit re-decrypted everything; (e) `sendMessage` awaited the full history
reload before clearing "Sending".

**Fixes:** commands → `async fn` (runtime thread pool); hydration newest-first
in parallel chunks of 6 with progressive `onPartial` flushes (newest messages
render immediately); query flipped to newest-250; module-scope plaintext cache
(`src/lib/chat-plaintext-cache.ts`) keyed to user+device, wiped on chat lock
(`use-workspace-lock`), logout (`auth-context`), and owner change; send now
fire-and-forgets the reconcile reload (local echo already on screen).

